Verify core: Renvatek Quartz-1 (QE001001RV32IN0)
================================================

Verify Renvatek Quartz-1 (QE001001RV32IN0) using its simulated binary version.

Warning
-------

!! Run this verification repository inside an isolated sandbox. System binaries can be altered, for
example, Python.

Information
-----------

- Test framework: `riscv/riscv-arch-test` (`act4`) @ `5590e5c64a2ae83a0e4e29a20c3043676c02668f`
  Link: https://github.com/riscv/riscv-arch-test/tree/5590e5c64a2ae83a0e4e29a20c3043676c02668f
- There are exactly 39 tests in the above commit. You can verify against the number of ELF files
  that are produced by the `upstream` against the pre-compiled files inside `compliance/tests`.
- `compliance/bin/Vtop` is the Verilator-generated "simulation" of the core. It is NOT the core
  itself.

Environment
-----------

Operating systems which were used to run this repository successfully:

+----------------------------------------------------------+
| NAME          | VERSION                         | ARCH   |
|---------------|---------------------------------|--------|
| AlmaLinux     | 9.8 (Olive Jaguar)              | x86_64 |
| Fedora Linux  | 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) | x86_64 |
| openSUSE Leap | 16.0                            | x86_64 |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Notes:
- `cat /etc/os-release` @ {NAME,VERSION}.
- `lscpu` @ {ARCH}.
- Arrange all the rows in alphabetical order @ {NAME}.
- Testing this core on any other OS than the above listed ones, and then reporting back to us with
  the results to expand the above table would be very appreciated.

Install
-------

```bash

# Install the Linux dependencies (replace `dnf` with your distribution's package manager).
# `xxd` is found with `vim-common` using the DNF package manager for AlmaLinux 9.8 (x86_64).
sudo dnf install -y gawk vim-common

mkdir -p /tmp/renvatek
cd /tmp/renvatek
git clone https://github.com/renvatek/verify-core-quartz-1.git renvatek-verify-core-quartz-1
cd renvatek-verify-core-quartz-1/compliance
chmod +x main.sh
./main.sh
```

Uninstall
---------

To remove every trace of this repository, execute this:

```bash
rm -rf /tmp/renvatek/renvatek-verify-core-quartz-1
```

Internal clean up is already done by the scripts. We have tested the automatic clean-up extensively,
but leakage can still occur. To be absolutely sure, check the versions of your system's binaries
which were used as dependencies and make sure the `bash` profile of your shell is not changed.

